==Maltese==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|mt|ar|[[إي]] [[و]]|tr=ʾī wa-||yes, by...}}, which is to be followed by someone or something to swear by. Common combinations are, for example, {{m|ar|إي والله|tr=ʾī wa-llāh||yes, by God}} or {{m|ar|إي وربي|tr=ʾī wa-rabbī||yes, by my Lord}}. Eventually the following word was left out. Compare the same in {{cog|acw|إيوه|tr=ʾīwa}} and similar forms in other dialects.

===Adverb===
{{head|mt|adverb}}

# [[yes]]

===See also===
* {{l|mt|forsi|gloss=maybe}}
* {{l|mt|le|gloss=no}}

